      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Plus, Unity still renders that tertiary camera view to the desktop, I found out that the view was yet a third VRChat \"eye\" or \"camera\" that had to render everything again rather than just mirroring one of the headset displays, which heavily burdens performance. That is the mirror I am talking about.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-01-14T22:18:10.869Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Even if it may be a tiny bit, the unity VR mirror takes an amount of cpu/gpu headroom and is no matter how insignificant, a burden to the performance of VR. Being able to disable it or (because of how buggy having the unity mirror hidden is) reduce its resolution to 640x480 as opposed to the 1080p minimum would improve performance drastically.",
